WEBVTT

﻿1
00:00:07.007 --> 00:00:10.010
- [laid-back jazz music playing]
- [chattering]

2
00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:18.074
Watch Online Movies and Series for FREE
www.osdb.link/lm

3
00:00:31.740 --> 00:00:32.741
[elevator dings]

4
00:00:36.161 --> 00:00:37.829
[Coop] Back when I was working
at Bailey Russell.

5
00:00:37.913 --> 00:00:40.499
I would start rolling calls
at 7:30 in the morning.

6
00:00:44.920 --> 00:00:48.757
One of the perks of being a thief
was that there was no one to call.

7
00:00:54.429 --> 00:00:55.430
[grunts]

8
00:01:00.561 --> 00:01:01.603
[sighs]

9
00:01:01.687 --> 00:01:03.772
And now. for the first time in my life.

10
00:01:03.856 --> 00:01:06.483
I had more empty hours
than I knew what to do with.

11
00:01:09.903 --> 00:01:13.448
- [woman screaming]
- [chain saw whirs]

12
00:01:24.293 --> 00:01:25.335
You're good.

13
00:01:26.795 --> 00:01:27.880
[tense music playing on screen]

14
00:01:27.963 --> 00:01:31.049
[chewing]

15
00:01:34.094 --> 00:01:35.262
[slurps]

16
00:01:40.475 --> 00:01:41.560
[Coop] It was quiet.

17
00:01:44.605 --> 00:01:46.565
And I had never done well with quiet.

18
00:01:47.441 --> 00:01:48.817
[podcasters chatting]

19
00:01:48.901 --> 00:01:50.360
[podcaster 1] I've never seen Peeping Tom.

20
00:01:50.444 --> 00:01:52.029
- Oh. Ben.
- You'd love it. Ben. You're the Peeper.

21
00:01:52.112 --> 00:01:53.280
[podcaster 2] Let me tell you

22
00:01:53.363 --> 00:01:55.449
- what the basic premise of this movie is.
- [Ben] Please.

23
00:01:55.532 --> 00:01:58.410
[podcaster 2] It's a guy who's obsessed
with the look on people's faces

24
00:01:58.493 --> 00:02:00.120
when they know they're about to die.

25
00:02:00.204 --> 00:02:04.082
He's a cameraman. and he builds a blade
into one of the legs of his tripod.

26
00:02:04.166 --> 00:02:06.460
[Coop] Mel used to complain
that I was never present in my own life.

27
00:02:06.543 --> 00:02:07.544
[podcasters continue]

28
00:02:07.628 --> 00:02:08.586
[sighs]

29
00:02:08.669 --> 00:02:12.674
[Coop] And with all this free time.
I somehow still wasn't.

30
00:02:12.758 --> 00:02:14.676
- [door closes]
- [Barney] You're late.

31
00:02:14.760 --> 00:02:15.802
Sorry.

32
00:02:16.637 --> 00:02:17.638
Is that a Bacon?

33
00:02:19.097 --> 00:02:20.474
It's a print. [sighs]

34
00:02:22.226 --> 00:02:23.227
[massager buzzes]

35
00:02:23.310 --> 00:02:28.482
So. you're processing hundreds
of thousands' worth of merchandise.

36
00:02:28.565 --> 00:02:29.691
How do you convert it?

37
00:02:31.235 --> 00:02:33.111
I have a guy. A fence.

38
00:02:33.195 --> 00:02:34.404
- And you trust him?
- [inhales sharply]

39
00:02:34.488 --> 00:02:36.031
To a point. yeah. [sighs]

40
00:02:36.114 --> 00:02:39.409
It's not like I can
put my business up for bid. [sighs]

41
00:02:39.493 --> 00:02:41.703
- I should meet him.
- Yeah. that's not happening.

42
00:02:41.787 --> 00:02:44.039
I haven't met him either.
if it makes you feel better.

43
00:02:44.122 --> 00:02:45.415
- Thanks. It doesn't.
- [Coop sighs]

44
00:02:45.499 --> 00:02:47.751
Coop. you're light. All right?

45
00:02:47.835 --> 00:02:50.629
You know your net carry has to be
in seven figures to cover your nut.

46
00:02:51.713 --> 00:02:55.008
You're gonna have to be more productive.
Bigger jobs or more of them.

47
00:02:55.092 --> 00:02:56.468
We're disciplined.

48
00:02:57.177 --> 00:03:01.056
We hit 14 houses across the county
over the last year without incident

49
00:03:01.139 --> 00:03:04.393
because we only target things
that won't be missed.

50
00:03:04.476 --> 00:03:07.104
Our whole business plan is based on
people not realizing they were robbed.

51
00:03:07.729 --> 00:03:09.940
- How are you showing income?
- Why do we have to show income?

52
00:03:10.023 --> 00:03:12.359
- Some of us pay taxes.
- I pay taxes!

53
00:03:12.442 --> 00:03:14.444
Don't get bent out of shape. all right?
I'm trying to help you.

54
00:03:14.528 --> 00:03:16.697
- I didn't ask for your help.
- Doesn't mean you don't need it.

55
00:03:16.780 --> 00:03:17.906
Where are you parking your money?

56
00:03:17.990 --> 00:03:20.409
I have small accounts
at a few different banks.

57
00:03:20.492 --> 00:03:21.910
Oh. good. So. there's a paper trail?

58
00:03:22.494 --> 00:03:23.495
Is he always like this?

59
00:03:23.579 --> 00:03:24.997
No. Sometimes he overreacts.

60
00:03:25.080 --> 00:03:26.623
Look. Coop. just…
just humor me. all right?

61
00:03:26.707 --> 00:03:30.502
So. just tell me. what was the plan
for when big ticket items come up. hmm?

62
00:03:30.586 --> 00:03:32.713
You can't pay Princeton
with a brown bag of cash.

63
00:03:32.796 --> 00:03:36.175
Come on. Coop. You know all this.
What did you think you were gonna do?

64
00:03:36.258 --> 00:03:38.093
It was only supposed to be
a stopgap measure.

65
00:03:38.177 --> 00:03:39.136
So. what happened?

66
00:03:39.720 --> 00:03:40.888
Turns out. we're good at it.

67
00:03:40.971 --> 00:03:43.932
[chuckles] Not from where I'm standing.

68
00:03:44.016 --> 00:03:45.767
Fuck you! Why is he even here?

69
00:03:45.851 --> 00:03:47.060
- Why am I here?
- Yeah.

70
00:03:47.144 --> 00:03:49.021
I'm here for him. all right?

71
00:03:49.104 --> 00:03:52.357
Because I was keeping him out of trouble
long before you ever came along.

72
00:03:52.441 --> 00:03:53.942
- [scoffs]
- We're gonna have to wash the money.

73
00:03:54.026 --> 00:03:55.027
Oh. you're gonna wash it?

74
00:03:55.110 --> 00:03:57.696
That means make it seem
like it comes from legitimate sources.

75
00:03:57.779 --> 00:03:59.698
Yeah. I know what money laundering is.

76
00:03:59.781 --> 00:04:02.993
I'm just shocked that a tight-ass suit
like you knows how to do it.

77
00:04:03.577 --> 00:04:04.745
You know. I liked you a lot better

78
00:04:04.828 --> 00:04:06.788
when you were just
Nick's inappropriately hot housekeeper.

79
00:04:06.872 --> 00:04:07.873
Hey!

80
00:04:07.956 --> 00:04:08.957
Coop…

81
00:04:10.918 --> 00:04:13.587
you remember Brett Sutter
from my PwC days?

82
00:04:14.087 --> 00:04:15.088
Didn't he get fired?

83
00:04:15.172 --> 00:04:19.468
Well. he left to work with less.
uh. palatable clients. right?

84
00:04:19.551 --> 00:04:21.762
The kind that primarily deal
in untraceable funds.

85
00:04:21.845 --> 00:04:23.388
I'm pretty sure he can set us up.

86
00:04:23.472 --> 00:04:25.432
Now. we convert the cash into crypto.

87
00:04:25.516 --> 00:04:27.851
tumble it between wallets
and generate fake invoices

88
00:04:27.935 --> 00:04:29.978
to create evidence
of a legitimate revenue stream.

89
00:04:30.562 --> 00:04:32.648
Congratulations.
I'm your business manager again.

90
00:04:33.357 --> 00:04:34.358
What's his end?

91
00:04:34.441 --> 00:04:37.110
I don't know. My guess. 20%.

92
00:04:37.194 --> 00:04:39.154
Twenty percent? Fuck that. [chuckles]

93
00:04:39.238 --> 00:04:40.239
That's off the gross.

94
00:04:40.322 --> 00:04:43.825
Listen. if you guys wanna trust
some scumbag with your money. that's fine.

95
00:04:43.909 --> 00:04:46.578
- [Barney sighs]
- He's not coming anywhere near mine.

96
00:04:51.083 --> 00:04:52.668
Well. she's a bright ray
of sunshine. isn't she?

97
00:04:52.751 --> 00:04:53.836
Barney. what are you doing?

98
00:04:54.753 --> 00:04:55.754
What are you talking about?

99
00:04:55.838 --> 00:04:57.339
You shouldn't be getting involved in this.

100
00:04:58.465 --> 00:04:59.925
You were my biggest client.

101
00:05:00.843 --> 00:05:03.220
Are you looking to get back
into legitimate business anytime soon?

102
00:05:03.303 --> 00:05:04.680
No.

103
00:05:06.431 --> 00:05:08.016
Then I'm getting involved.

104
00:05:08.100 --> 00:05:09.268
I'll set the meeting.

105
00:05:11.144 --> 00:05:13.230
[sighs heavily]

106
00:05:15.732 --> 00:05:16.733
[groans]

107
00:05:17.317 --> 00:05:20.362
[buzzing]

108
00:05:20.445 --> 00:05:21.446
[groans]

109
00:05:21.530 --> 00:05:23.907
[theme song playing]

110
00:05:26.660 --> 00:05:31.373
♪ A paper shadow in a house of stone ♪

111
00:05:32.124 --> 00:05:37.171
♪ The wooden flag
Of a drifting dreamboat ♪

112
00:05:37.254 --> 00:05:41.383
♪ I never knew
How far the ride was gonna go ♪

113
00:05:41.466 --> 00:05:44.928
♪ Till I looked back at the smoke ♪

114
00:05:45.012 --> 00:05:49.474
♪ You can't keep up with the Joneses ♪

115
00:05:50.267 --> 00:05:55.105
♪ Don't wanna run for the roses ♪

116
00:05:55.189 --> 00:06:00.360
♪ I got my pocket of posies ♪

117
00:06:00.444 --> 00:06:02.946
♪ Sometimes I wonder why ♪

118
00:06:03.030 --> 00:06:05.073
♪ Sometimes I wonder why ♪

119
00:06:05.574 --> 00:06:10.162
♪ I just don't run with the Joneses ♪

120
00:06:10.787 --> 00:06:15.834
♪ Don't wanna smell the dying roses ♪

121
00:06:15.918 --> 00:06:20.923
♪ I got my pocket full of posies ♪

122
00:06:21.006 --> 00:06:25.969
♪ I don't keep up with the Joneses ♪

123
00:06:41.235 --> 00:06:44.488
[breathing heavily]

124
00:06:51.203 --> 00:06:55.332
[blowing]

125
00:07:00.379 --> 00:07:02.422
[alarm ringing]

126
00:07:02.506 --> 00:07:05.217
[groans. exhales sharply]

127
00:07:06.385 --> 00:07:09.805
[breathes heavily]

128
00:07:10.681 --> 00:07:12.391
[blows]

129
00:07:12.474 --> 00:07:14.226
[sighs]

130
00:07:16.937 --> 00:07:18.230
Uh. hello?

131
00:07:18.730 --> 00:07:20.148
- We're going to be late.
- Good morning.

132
00:07:20.232 --> 00:07:21.567
No. you're not. You're never late.

133
00:07:22.150 --> 00:07:25.320
Hey. are you gonna. um.
check your admissions portal today?

134
00:07:25.404 --> 00:07:28.115
- Why?
- What do you mean. "why"?

135
00:07:28.198 --> 00:07:30.117
You're supposed to hear from Princeton
any day now.

136
00:07:30.200 --> 00:07:31.326
Okay. Mom.

137
00:07:32.119 --> 00:07:33.412
Don't "Okay. Mom" me.

138
00:07:33.495 --> 00:07:34.913
Okay. Mom.

139
00:07:35.789 --> 00:07:37.666
- All right. I see what you did there.
- Did you?

140
00:07:37.749 --> 00:07:39.626
[chuckling] Irony is your love language.

141
00:07:39.710 --> 00:07:41.211
And I love you too.

142
00:07:51.471 --> 00:07:53.891
And then. depression set in.

143
00:07:55.392 --> 00:07:57.394
[pensive music playing]

144
00:07:58.270 --> 00:07:59.396
[coffee machine whirs]

145
00:08:49.530 --> 00:08:51.782
[dance music playing on TV]

146
00:09:00.374 --> 00:09:01.542
[music continues]

147
00:09:01.625 --> 00:09:03.252
[doorbell rings]

148
00:09:09.508 --> 00:09:12.219
[pensive music playing]

149
00:09:43.542 --> 00:09:45.544
- [squelching]
- [gasps. groans]

150
00:09:47.045 --> 00:09:48.463
[exhales sharply]

151
00:09:49.381 --> 00:09:50.382
[sighs]

152
00:09:52.342 --> 00:09:53.468
Fuck.

153
00:09:58.140 --> 00:09:59.683
No. no. You don't wanna see that.

154
00:09:59.766 --> 00:10:01.643
It's split-level and dated.

155
00:10:02.186 --> 00:10:04.521
[knocks on door]

156
00:10:04.605 --> 00:10:06.231
Holly. can you give me a second?

157
00:10:07.191 --> 00:10:09.484
Esperanza. can you get that?

158
00:10:09.568 --> 00:10:11.612
We're in the bath. Miss Samantha!

159
00:10:11.695 --> 00:10:13.071
[sighs]

160
00:10:13.155 --> 00:10:16.491
Well. I went to a…
a dinner party there two years ago.

161
00:10:16.575 --> 00:10:20.329
and the space felt really great
and big and open.

162
00:10:21.205 --> 00:10:22.706
Okay. Great.

163
00:10:22.789 --> 00:10:25.334
I will see you there tomorrow.

164
00:10:26.919 --> 00:10:28.754
9:30. Right. Text me your coffee order.

165
00:10:28.837 --> 00:10:31.006
- All right. Bye.
- New business?

166
00:10:31.089 --> 00:10:32.966
- Yeah.
- Hell yeah.

167
00:10:33.050 --> 00:10:34.968
- Thanks for that. And for this.
- Mmm.

168
00:10:35.052 --> 00:10:37.012
Hey. it's just my way
of saying "Thank you."

169
00:10:37.095 --> 00:10:38.972
[chuckles] It's a pretty big bouquet.

170
00:10:39.056 --> 00:10:40.641
It's a pretty big house.

171
00:10:43.519 --> 00:10:45.312
Owen. you're very charming…

172
00:10:45.395 --> 00:10:46.563
And humble. Right?

173
00:10:47.648 --> 00:10:48.982
But I'm not going to date you.

174
00:10:49.066 --> 00:10:53.278
Wow. Usually people wait for me
to ask them out before they turn me down.

175
00:10:53.362 --> 00:10:55.489
Look. I could see how I might seem to you

176
00:10:55.572 --> 00:10:58.242
like someone who has
their life together and. I mean…

177
00:10:58.325 --> 00:11:00.285
- No. [chuckles] Not really.
- Oh.

178
00:11:00.369 --> 00:11:02.454
I mean. everything you've been through.
I'm sure you're a hot mess.

179
00:11:02.538 --> 00:11:05.082
- Well. that's a fair assessment.
- And it's very sexy.

180
00:11:05.165 --> 00:11:08.126
So you just figured I was vulnerable.
and lonely. and horny.

181
00:11:08.210 --> 00:11:10.087
and desperate to please?

182
00:11:10.921 --> 00:11:12.464
No. that's me.

183
00:11:12.548 --> 00:11:14.550
[both chuckle]

184
00:11:14.633 --> 00:11:17.219
No. I figured you'd have
no patience for bullshit.

185
00:11:17.302 --> 00:11:21.056
And you'd be open and honest with me.
the way no one else around here is.

186
00:11:21.139 --> 00:11:23.892
Well. I appreciate that.

187
00:11:23.976 --> 00:11:27.479
And in that spirit.
I'd just like to reiterate

188
00:11:27.563 --> 00:11:30.274
- that I am not going to date--
- And you're so hot.

189
00:11:30.357 --> 00:11:32.568
- [chuckles]
- It's crazy. really. We can't deny that.

190
00:11:32.651 --> 00:11:36.613
Thank you. But sadly.
I am a committed spinster now.

191
00:11:37.698 --> 00:11:39.533
- I get it. really I do. I do.
- Mm-hmm.

192
00:11:39.616 --> 00:11:41.493
Now. just give me a minute
'cause I'm gonna tell you

193
00:11:41.577 --> 00:11:43.287
all the reasons why
that's a terrible idea.

194
00:11:43.370 --> 00:11:44.746
- Okay. [chuckles]
- Terrible idea.

195
00:11:44.830 --> 00:11:46.081
- Good night.
- Thirty seconds.

196
00:11:46.164 --> 00:11:47.457
Good night. Owen.

197
00:11:50.085 --> 00:11:51.628
It's Ashe.

198
00:11:56.258 --> 00:11:58.135
[chattering]

199
00:12:11.231 --> 00:12:13.442
- [pop music plays on headphones]
- You know that girl?

200
00:12:14.818 --> 00:12:16.278
Started at Mayfield last week.

201
00:12:17.404 --> 00:12:20.282
Her dad is the superrich guy who threw
the thing Mom and Dad went to.

202
00:12:20.365 --> 00:12:21.533
Hmm.

203
00:12:22.117 --> 00:12:23.160
Is she your year?

204
00:12:23.660 --> 00:12:24.661
[Hunter] Yeah.

205
00:12:26.538 --> 00:12:27.956
Well. go talk to her.

206
00:12:29.958 --> 00:12:30.959
Why?

207
00:12:31.043 --> 00:12:33.378
Because she's alone
and it's what people do.

208
00:12:36.131 --> 00:12:37.758
She looks busy.

209
00:12:39.801 --> 00:12:41.220
Hey! New girl!

210
00:12:41.929 --> 00:12:42.930
This is Hunter.

211
00:12:43.013 --> 00:12:44.473
Do you wanna talk to him?

212
00:12:48.393 --> 00:12:49.520
You're welcome.

213
00:13:06.870 --> 00:13:08.539
Hunter Cooper. right?

214
00:13:08.622 --> 00:13:10.541
I think we have bio together.

215
00:13:13.210 --> 00:13:14.878
I'm Delilah Ashe.

216
00:13:14.962 --> 00:13:16.964
Your sister is a lot. huh?

217
00:13:17.673 --> 00:13:19.508
She's also kind of a know-it-all.

218
00:13:19.591 --> 00:13:20.592
And surprisingly messy.

219
00:13:20.676 --> 00:13:22.344
There's like. hair. everywhere.

220
00:13:22.427 --> 00:13:23.428
All the time.

221
00:13:26.890 --> 00:13:28.267
W-What are you drawing?

222
00:13:30.894 --> 00:13:32.020
You.

223
00:13:32.729 --> 00:13:35.232
- That's really good.
- [chuckles] Thanks.

224
00:13:35.315 --> 00:13:36.733
Where were you before this?

225
00:13:36.817 --> 00:13:38.026
Schloss Krumbach.

226
00:13:38.110 --> 00:13:39.945
It's a boarding school in Austria.

227
00:13:40.654 --> 00:13:41.864
Why Austria?

228
00:13:41.947 --> 00:13:44.032
No idea. You'd have to ask my father.

229
00:13:44.116 --> 00:13:47.160
And I'm the last person
who's gonna cape for Austria.

230
00:13:47.244 --> 00:13:49.621
Shitty food and German is
an impossible language.

231
00:13:49.705 --> 00:13:52.708
[chuckles] So why'd you move here?

232
00:13:52.791 --> 00:13:54.042
As far as I can tell.

233
00:13:54.126 --> 00:13:57.629
my father's decided to try his hand
at actually being a parent.

234
00:13:57.713 --> 00:13:58.881
And I guess step one is.

235
00:13:58.964 --> 00:14:02.759
like. completely uprooting
and disrupting your daughter's life.

236
00:14:05.179 --> 00:14:07.306
- And your mom?
- She died when I was eight.

237
00:14:10.309 --> 00:14:11.435
I'm sorry.

238
00:14:14.229 --> 00:14:17.065
Yeah. the dead mother is
kind of a conversation killer.

239
00:14:21.069 --> 00:14:22.696
[stammers] Are you here alone?

240
00:14:22.779 --> 00:14:26.158
No. All my new friends
should be getting here any second.

241
00:14:27.117 --> 00:14:28.368
[both chuckle]

242
00:14:28.869 --> 00:14:30.037
[inhales deeply]

243
00:14:31.413 --> 00:14:33.165
So are you gonna sit down. or what?

244
00:14:40.631 --> 00:14:41.632
Hey.

245
00:14:41.715 --> 00:14:42.716
What are you doing?

246
00:14:42.799 --> 00:14:44.343
- We have a court in ten minutes.
- [sighs]

247
00:14:44.426 --> 00:14:45.427
You have your racket?

248
00:14:45.511 --> 00:14:47.679
Maybe put on some clothes?

249
00:14:48.722 --> 00:14:50.974
Come on. Dad.
Princeton has already made its decision.

250
00:14:51.058 --> 00:14:53.143
Okay. one more session
isn't gonna make a difference.

251
00:14:53.227 --> 00:14:55.979
I'm not worried about Princeton.
I'm worried about me.

252
