00:24:45.402 --> 00:24:48.071
Well. not me.
For one or two companies I own. [sighs]

500
00:24:48.155 --> 00:24:51.366
And I remit taxable payments
to your company.

501
00:24:51.450 --> 00:24:52.951
Minus my commission.

502
00:24:53.035 --> 00:24:54.578
- And how much is that?
- Thirty.

503
00:24:55.746 --> 00:24:57.289
Bullshit. Twenty.

504
00:24:58.081 --> 00:24:59.666
Thirty is industry-standard.

505
00:24:59.750 --> 00:25:03.003
Oh. [stammers] I must've missed that
in the newsletter.

506
00:25:07.799 --> 00:25:10.177
[scoffs] I'll do it for a quarter.

507
00:25:12.513 --> 00:25:13.639
[inhales deeply] Deal.

508
00:25:13.722 --> 00:25:15.307
What's the lead time on this?

509
00:25:16.099 --> 00:25:17.518
After we set up your dummy wallets…

510
00:25:17.601 --> 00:25:18.727
- [fingers snap]
- …like that.

511
00:25:21.104 --> 00:25:22.523
I'm gonna get you boys some whiskeys.

512
00:25:22.606 --> 00:25:25.651
We can get into the. uh. dirty details.
all right?

513
00:25:26.360 --> 00:25:28.904
[mysterious music playing]

514
00:25:31.615 --> 00:25:33.325
I'll come up with something else.

515
00:25:37.663 --> 00:25:38.914
[Samantha] It's no problem. Marcia.

516
00:25:38.997 --> 00:25:40.958
[Marcia. on phone]
I don't wanna be difficult. but…

517
00:25:41.041 --> 00:25:43.710
Please. you're not being difficult.
You mean. you want what you want.

518
00:25:43.794 --> 00:25:45.212
I mean. I love the house.

519
00:25:45.295 --> 00:25:47.506
but. at this price point.
I just need to be reassured

520
00:25:47.589 --> 00:25:49.758
that we're not gonna be limited
by zoning restrictions

521
00:25:49.842 --> 00:25:52.761
once we start renovating.
How do we get clarity on that?

522
00:25:52.845 --> 00:25:56.223
You know what? Let me do some digging
on my end and I'll get back to you soon.

523
00:25:56.306 --> 00:25:58.141
- Okay. great. That'd be wonderful.
- Okay.

524
00:25:58.225 --> 00:25:59.935
- Thank you.
- Yep. Okay. bye.

525
00:26:00.018 --> 00:26:01.019
Bye.

526
00:26:01.854 --> 00:26:04.356
[pony blusters]

527
00:26:09.903 --> 00:26:10.904
[sighs]

528
00:26:14.199 --> 00:26:15.701
- Fuck it.
- [tires screech]

529
00:26:15.784 --> 00:26:16.994
[playful music playing]

530
00:26:19.997 --> 00:26:22.082
[partygoers chattering]

531
00:26:37.848 --> 00:26:39.850
I mean. he didn't even…

532
00:26:40.767 --> 00:26:41.768
Oh. my God.

533
00:26:41.852 --> 00:26:44.396
[wistful music playing]

534
00:26:45.272 --> 00:26:47.774
- Did you know she was coming?
- I sure didn't.

535
00:26:48.859 --> 00:26:50.694
I definitely didn't ask.

536
00:26:51.445 --> 00:26:53.280
- Babe. don't.
- Just give me a second.

537
00:26:56.450 --> 00:26:58.243
[Maggie] Sam. wait.

538
00:26:58.327 --> 00:26:59.369
Sam!

539
00:27:00.162 --> 00:27:02.122
Was Henry the only kid in class
who wasn't invited?

540
00:27:02.206 --> 00:27:05.000
It wasn't meant to be such a big thing.
It just… It kind of blew up.

541
00:27:05.083 --> 00:27:06.585
He just lost his father. Maggie.

542
00:27:06.668 --> 00:27:09.171
- Do you have even an ounce of compassion?
- Of course I do.

543
00:27:09.254 --> 00:27:10.964
Look. it's a complicated situation.

544
00:27:11.048 --> 00:27:12.591
There are a lot of raw feelings.

545
00:27:12.674 --> 00:27:14.718
Oh. my God. He is a five-year-old boy.

546
00:27:15.219 --> 00:27:16.762
No one would've cared if he was here.

547
00:27:16.845 --> 00:27:18.680
It wasn't Henry we were worried about.

548
00:27:20.390 --> 00:27:21.808
I could've sent him with someone else.

549
00:27:21.892 --> 00:27:23.810
What was I supposed to do?
Invite him and not you?

550
00:27:23.894 --> 00:27:25.229
Yes!

551
00:27:25.312 --> 00:27:27.731
Because that would've
only been moderately shitty of you.

552
00:27:27.814 --> 00:27:29.942
Instead. you decide
to exclude a five-year-old boy

553
00:27:30.025 --> 00:27:31.735
who's still reeling
from his father's suicide.

554
00:27:31.818 --> 00:27:33.403
- Sam--
- He thinks Daisy is his best friend.

555
00:27:33.487 --> 00:27:36.448
I don't think you appreciate
the position you've put us all in.

556
00:27:38.659 --> 00:27:39.743
This is because of Mel.

557
00:27:39.826 --> 00:27:40.994
That's not what I said.

558
00:27:41.078 --> 00:27:44.414
Jesus Christ. it feels like
I'm in high school all over again.

559
00:27:44.498 --> 00:27:46.625
Did you frame someone for murder
in high school?

560
00:27:48.001 --> 00:27:49.086
Fuck you. Maggie.

561
00:27:50.420 --> 00:27:52.589
And you can tell yourself
all the lies you want.

562
00:27:52.673 --> 00:27:53.799
but there's no version of this

563
00:27:53.882 --> 00:27:56.093
where you didn't just take a cheap shot
at a little boy.

564
00:27:56.885 --> 00:27:58.470
He didn't do anything to anyone.

565
00:27:58.554 --> 00:27:59.555
I know.

566
00:28:01.139 --> 00:28:04.393
- I wish it didn't have to be this way.
- That's the thing. Maggie.

567
00:28:04.476 --> 00:28:05.727
It doesn't.

568
00:28:07.771 --> 00:28:09.648
[pensive music playing]

569
00:28:17.698 --> 00:28:19.616
[metal jingling]

570
00:28:19.700 --> 00:28:23.620
[dog panting. groaning]

571
00:28:30.085 --> 00:28:32.212
[playfully suspenseful music playing]

572
00:28:38.468 --> 00:28:39.511
- Hey. buddy.
- [barking]

573
00:28:39.595 --> 00:28:40.762
[gasps]

574
00:28:41.680 --> 00:28:43.557
[barking continues]

575
00:28:46.101 --> 00:28:47.102
[barking continues]

576
00:28:47.186 --> 00:28:48.353
All right.

577
00:28:50.230 --> 00:28:52.774
Easy. Hi.

578
00:28:52.858 --> 00:28:55.485
Hey. buddy. Are you friendly?

579
00:28:56.528 --> 00:28:57.863
Are you friend…

580
00:28:59.156 --> 00:29:00.741
Hey! Hey!

581
00:29:01.658 --> 00:29:03.410
Go shit in your own yard!

582
00:29:03.493 --> 00:29:04.912
Shoo!

583
00:29:04.995 --> 00:29:06.580
Get the fuck outta here.

584
00:29:07.623 --> 00:29:08.832
Shoo!

585
00:29:08.916 --> 00:29:10.459
Fucking dumbass.

586
00:29:11.210 --> 00:29:12.836
Yeah. you better run.

587
00:29:18.467 --> 00:29:21.094
- Mel. Hi.
- Hi. Brienne.

588
00:29:21.178 --> 00:29:22.888
This is a surprise.

589
00:29:23.889 --> 00:29:25.682
Hey. did you just work out or something?

590
00:29:25.766 --> 00:29:26.850
No.

591
00:29:28.352 --> 00:29:30.395
W-Well. you just have
a little. um. moisture.

592
00:29:30.479 --> 00:29:31.813
- Oh.
- Moisture right there.

593
00:29:31.897 --> 00:29:34.691
- Yeah. yeah. yeah. right there.
- Uh. just walked all the way over.

594
00:29:34.775 --> 00:29:35.984
- [chuckles]
- Okay.

595
00:29:36.693 --> 00:29:38.111
Hi. Is… Is everything okay?

596
00:29:38.195 --> 00:29:41.031
Um. yeah. Ish. Um…

597
00:29:41.114 --> 00:29:43.575
[clicks tongue]
Did you and Clay happen to just buy a dog?

598
00:29:43.659 --> 00:29:44.660
Arlo.

599
00:29:45.202 --> 00:29:46.745
Yes. We didn't buy him.

600
00:29:46.828 --> 00:29:48.163
We rescued him.

601
00:29:48.247 --> 00:29:52.125
He was sent back twice.
and then given to a kill shelter.

602
00:29:52.209 --> 00:29:53.418
I mean. can you believe that?

603
00:29:53.502 --> 00:29:54.962
Oh. Yes.

604
00:29:55.045 --> 00:29:56.046
- Uh. no.
- [sighs]

605
00:29:56.713 --> 00:29:59.383
- The thing is. your dog…
- Arlo.

606
00:29:59.466 --> 00:30:03.220
- Arlo is using my backyard as a toilet.
- Yeah.

607
00:30:03.303 --> 00:30:05.430
Oh. Really?

608
00:30:06.265 --> 00:30:08.725
[chuckles] Well. I'm sorry about that.

609
00:30:09.768 --> 00:30:13.105
I'm thrilled that he's found
his forever home.

610
00:30:13.188 --> 00:30:16.775
but if you could just make sure
he stays in his forever yard…

611
00:30:17.401 --> 00:30:18.902
We will definitely try.

612
00:30:19.778 --> 00:30:22.322
The thing with mastiffs is
that they tend to wander.

613
00:30:22.406 --> 00:30:26.827
and they kind of prefer to. like.
roam free. you know?

614
00:30:29.079 --> 00:30:32.249
In the English countryside
in the 19th century.

615
00:30:32.332 --> 00:30:35.169
but we're in Westchester now.

616
00:30:37.921 --> 00:30:40.716
Yeah. I will. um. do my best.

617
00:30:40.799 --> 00:30:42.342
[chuckles]

618
00:30:42.426 --> 00:30:43.468
Thank you.

619
00:30:46.638 --> 00:30:48.307
Thanks for coming by!

620
00:30:59.902 --> 00:31:01.904
[melancholy music playing]

621
00:31:35.521 --> 00:31:36.939
[chuckles]

622
00:31:44.154 --> 00:31:45.531
[school bell rings]

623
00:31:45.614 --> 00:31:47.157
["Your One Way Street"
playing on headphones]

624
00:31:47.241 --> 00:31:51.954
♪ Feeling something's leaving ♪

625
00:31:52.037 --> 00:31:56.625
♪ But I can't change what's happening ♪

626
00:31:56.708 --> 00:31:57.709
[music stops]

627
00:31:58.627 --> 00:31:59.920
Hey. [chuckles]

628
00:32:00.921 --> 00:32:02.130
You look different.

629
00:32:02.714 --> 00:32:04.091
[sighs] No shit.

630
00:32:04.174 --> 00:32:07.886
[chuckles] I'm also itchy
and lightly nauseous.

631
00:32:07.970 --> 00:32:09.263
I don't know why. [sighs]

632
00:32:09.346 --> 00:32:11.682
It's just some… [stammers]
…stuffy elitist prep school.

633
00:32:11.765 --> 00:32:14.142
[chuckles] No offense.

634
00:32:14.935 --> 00:32:17.271
- They're gonna judge me.
- No. You'll be great.

635
00:32:17.354 --> 00:32:19.022
You think so?

636
00:32:20.190 --> 00:32:21.692
[stammers] Not at the interview part.

637
00:32:21.775 --> 00:32:24.069
- But at the teaching. yeah.
- [chuckles] Okay.

638
00:32:24.152 --> 00:32:25.571
- Hey. Hunter.
- Hey.

639
00:32:27.447 --> 00:32:28.448
Wassup?

640
00:32:28.532 --> 00:32:30.325
Delilah. this is my aunt. Ali.

641
00:32:30.409 --> 00:32:31.410
The singer?

642
00:32:31.493 --> 00:32:33.745
[gasps] You talked about me? Aw.

643
00:32:33.829 --> 00:32:34.830
It's nice to meet you.

644
00:32:34.913 --> 00:32:36.415
You too.

645
00:32:36.498 --> 00:32:39.084
- [Ali] Delilah. [chuckles]
- [Delilah chuckles]

646
00:32:40.335 --> 00:32:41.336
Cool.

647
00:32:41.420 --> 00:32:46.008
Well. I am just gonna go stand over there
and sweat my balls off.

648
00:32:46.091 --> 00:32:47.509
[Ali. Delilah chuckle]

649
00:32:49.678 --> 00:32:51.054
Is she okay?

650
00:32:51.763 --> 00:32:53.182
[stammers] Unclear.

651
00:32:53.932 --> 00:32:55.017
So this is a lot.

652
00:32:55.100 --> 00:32:58.812
but my dad got me insane floor seats
to see The Walkmen at the Beacon tonight.

653
00:32:58.896 --> 00:33:00.397
You're kidding. I love The Walkmen.

654
00:33:00.480 --> 00:33:04.902
He's feeling guilty for all the moving
around. so he's trying to buy me friends.

655
00:33:04.985 --> 00:33:05.986
[inhales sharply]

656
00:33:06.069 --> 00:33:08.655
So I guess my question for you is.
are you for sale?

657
00:33:08.739 --> 00:33:10.908
Oh. yeah. You had me at floor seats.

658
00:33:11.658 --> 00:33:13.785
Great. We'll pick you up at 5:00.

659
00:33:13.869 --> 00:33:15.329
Give me your info.

660
00:33:20.334 --> 00:33:21.335
Hey. Hunter.

661
00:33:21.418 --> 00:33:22.419
Hey.

662
00:33:23.712 --> 00:33:25.672
Hi. I'm Morgan.

663
00:33:25.756 --> 00:33:26.798
Are you new here?

664
00:33:26.882 --> 00:33:28.342
Yes. I'm Delilah.

665
00:33:28.425 --> 00:33:29.676
I just transferred in.

666
00:33:29.760 --> 00:33:32.304
With three months left of school?

667
00:33:33.055 --> 00:33:35.974
I like to up the degree of difficulty
wherever I can.

668
00:33:39.520 --> 00:33:40.854
I love your boots.

669
00:33:41.438 --> 00:33:42.439
Thanks.

670
00:33:44.191 --> 00:33:45.317
Ms. Cooper?

671
00:33:45.400 --> 00:33:46.860
Dr. Seelbach is ready for you.

672
00:33:46.944 --> 00:33:48.278
[Ali] Okay.

673
00:33:48.362 --> 00:33:49.655
Hunter?

674
00:33:49.738 --> 00:33:51.657
Hey. um. do I have anything in my teeth?

675
00:33:52.157 --> 00:33:54.117
- [Hunter] All clear.
- [Ali] Are you sure?

676
00:33:54.201 --> 00:33:56.161
- 'Cause I had kale salad for lunch…
- Bye.

677
00:33:56.245 --> 00:33:58.205
…with a little tuna. Um. how's my breath?

678
00:33:58.288 --> 00:33:59.540
[exhales deeply]

679
00:34:00.290 --> 00:34:01.625
Good luck in there.

680
00:34:02.543 --> 00:34:03.836
Good luck out here.

681
00:34:06.338 --> 00:34:08.549
[door opens. closes]

682
00:34:08.632 --> 00:34:10.092
[school bell rings]

683
00:34:10.175 --> 00:34:11.969
["Messy" playing on radio]

684
00:34:12.052 --> 00:34:14.137
♪ And then I'm too fucking clean ♪

685
00:34:14.221 --> 00:34:18.641
♪ You told me. "Get a job"
Then you ask where the hell I've been ♪

686
00:34:18.725 --> 00:34:20.518
♪ And I'm too perfect ♪

687
00:34:20.601 --> 00:34:22.980
♪ Till I open my big mouth ♪

688
00:34:23.063 --> 00:34:25.148
♪ I want to be me ♪

689
00:34:25.232 --> 00:34:27.317
♪ Is that not allowed? ♪

690
00:34:27.400 --> 00:34:29.277
- ♪ And I'm too clever ♪
- [song stops]

691
00:34:46.587 --> 00:34:50.340
- Surprise!
- [cheering. laughing]

692
00:34:52.050 --> 00:34:53.677
- [Coop exclaims]
- [Mel] You got in.

693
00:34:53.760 --> 00:34:55.929
- I never doubted you for a second.
- [Ron] Way to go. honey.

694
00:34:56.013 --> 00:34:58.640
- [laughs] Cupcakes.
- Baby. have a cupcake.

695
00:34:58.724 --> 00:34:59.766
- [laughing]
- Wait. how…

696
00:34:59.850 --> 00:35:01.685
How could you know that I got in?

697
00:35:01.768 --> 00:35:04.104
I checked your Common app.

698
00:35:04.188 --> 00:35:07.399
You left your password on our iCloud.

699
00:35:07.482 --> 00:35:08.901
You had no right to do that.

700
00:35:08.984 --> 00:35:12.321
Hey. she just wanted to get ahead of it
so we could surprise you.

701
00:35:13.488 --> 00:35:14.907
Why don't you seem excited?

702
00:35:14.990 --> 00:35:16.825
Well. she's probably in shock.

703
00:35:16.909 --> 00:35:18.785
[chuckles] I mean. look at this fuss.

704
00:35:19.411 --> 00:35:21.455
Hey. what's going on?

705
00:35:22.915 --> 00:35:25.459
[sighs] I was gonna talk
to you guys about this.

706
00:35:25.542 --> 00:35:26.543
About what?

707
00:35:28.212 --> 00:35:29.213
[sighs]

708
00:35:29.296 --> 00:35:31.757
I'm not going to Princeton.
[breathes shakily]

709
00:35:31.840 --> 00:35:32.966
I already declined.

710
00:35:33.884 --> 00:35:34.885
[sighs]

711
00:35:39.473 --> 00:35:40.641
[singsongy] Surprise.

712
00:35:43.852 --> 00:35:45.437
- [Mel] Tori.
- Whoa. whoa. Mel.

713
00:35:45.521 --> 00:35:46.522
[Mel] No.

714
00:35:47.064 --> 00:35:48.106
Baby. talk to us.

715
00:35:48.190 --> 00:35:50.317
- What's going on?
- I told you. I declined the offer.

716
00:35:50.400 --> 00:35:52.402
What do you mean you declined the offer?
That's not funny.

717
00:35:52.486 --> 00:35:53.820
Do you see me laughing?

718
00:35:56.406 --> 00:35:59.284
If you were… [stammers] …having doubts.
why didn't you tell us?

719
00:35:59.368 --> 00:36:01.703
Because I knew it would
pretty much go like this.

720
00:36:01.787 --> 00:36:03.455
- Tori Cooper. you--
- Okay. Hey. [stammers] Hey.

721
00:36:03.539 --> 00:36:04.957
Hey. Let's calm down. please.

722
00:36:05.040 --> 00:36:07.626
- Did you know about this?
- Of course I didn't know about this.

723
00:36:07.709 --> 00:36:09.503
- What…
- What is happening here?

724
00:36:09.586 --> 00:36:11.421
- Did something happen?
- No.

725
00:36:11.505 --> 00:36:13.465
- What-What are you not telling us?
- Nothing. Mom.

726
00:36:13.549 --> 00:36:15.634
You're just not accepting
what I am telling you.

727
00:36:15.717 --> 00:36:17.094
Of course I'm not accepting it.

728
00:36:17.177 --> 00:36:20.514
You just spent the last four years
working your ass off to get in.

729
00:36:20.597 --> 00:36:23.225
Now. suddenly overnight
you decide you don't wanna go?

730
00:36:23.308 --> 00:36:24.351
Is there another college

731
00:36:24.434 --> 00:36:25.936
- that you wanted to choose?
- What?

732
00:36:26.019 --> 00:36:27.980
No. I don't know if
I wanna go to college at all.

733
00:36:28.063 --> 00:36:30.357
[chuckling] Okay.

734
00:36:30.440 --> 00:36:32.025
I'm-I'm not following.

735
00:36:33.235 --> 00:36:35.445
Do you have any idea
what she's talking about?

736
00:36:35.529 --> 00:36:38.615
I'm making my way up to it.
Yes. I'm trying to figure it out.

737
00:36:38.699 --> 00:36:42.828
Tori. do you think you might be more
comfortable talking about it with me?

738
00:36:42.911 --> 00:36:44.955
- Mom.
- I'm just trying to help.

739
00:36:45.038 --> 00:36:46.623
No. thank you. We've got it.

740
00:36:46.707 --> 00:36:48.125
It doesn't look that way to me.

741
00:36:48.208 --> 00:36:49.501
- Okay. thanks.
- Wow.

742
00:36:49.585 --> 00:36:52.629
Guys. let's all push pause. huh?

743
00:36:53.172 --> 00:36:57.509
I-I-I get that you clearly have
a lot on your mind right now.

744
00:36:57.593 --> 00:37:01.263
Maybe you could've shared some of this
information with us a little bit earlier.

745
00:37:01.346 --> 00:37:04.600
But why don't we three go somewhere

746
00:37:04.683 --> 00:37:06.643
and sit down and try to figure out
what's going on?

747
00:37:06.727 --> 00:37:08.395
Nothing's going on.

748
00:37:08.478 --> 00:37:10.230
I'm just… [sighs]

749
00:37:10.772 --> 00:37:14.359
I'm not sure that I want the same things
that you guys want for me.

750
00:37:14.985 --> 00:37:18.530
Tori. [stammers] Us wanting you to go
to college isn't some outrageous thing.

751
00:37:18.614 --> 00:37:19.615
It's college.

752
00:37:19.698 --> 00:37:21.575
Everything has always been
about what you guys want.

753
00:37:21.658 --> 00:37:24.077
You've never once bothered
to ask me if it's what I wanted.

754
00:37:24.161 --> 00:37:25.412
Okay. [stammers] Okay.

755
00:37:25.495 --> 00:37:26.747
Uh. I'm sorry. all right?

756
00:37:26.830 --> 00:37:29.875
This is… This is us asking.
what-what do… what do you want?

757
00:37:32.669 --> 00:37:33.712
I don't know.

758
00:37:36.924 --> 00:37:38.926
- [sighs]
- Oh. my God.

759
00:37:44.848 --> 00:37:45.849
[quietly] Are you pregnant?

760
00:37:45.933 --> 00:37:47.100
Fuck. Mom!

761
00:37:48.268 --> 00:37:49.269
Hey. I…

762
00:37:49.353 --> 00:37:51.480
- I'm talking to you.
- Pregnant? Are you fucking serious?

763
00:37:51.563 --> 00:37:53.273
I'm sorry. It just came out.

764
00:37:53.357 --> 00:37:55.484
- Can you wait a minute? Hey.
- Stop. Mom.

765
00:37:55.567 --> 00:37:57.819
- [Mel screams] Oh. my God. Tori!
- [screams]

766
00:37:57.903 --> 00:37:59.404
- [Coop] Jesus Christ.
- Oh. my goodness. Sweetie.

767
00:37:59.488 --> 00:38:01.156
- Jesus! Are you all right?
- I'm fine.

768
00:38:01.240 --> 00:38:02.866
- Did you hit your head?
- It's fine. I'm fine.

769
00:38:02.950 --> 00:38:05.077
- Yeah.
- [Mel] So sorry. sweetheart.

770
00:38:05.160 --> 00:38:07.538
Okay. can we just talk about
something else. please?

771
00:38:08.747 --> 00:38:10.457
[breathes heavily]

772
00:38:10.541 --> 00:38:11.542
[Coop sighs]

773
00:38:12.376 --> 00:38:14.461
Hey. uh…

774
00:38:16.505 --> 00:38:19.716
I'm gonna be teaching at Mayfield now.

775
00:38:19.800 --> 00:38:20.926
[Hunter] You got the job?

776
00:38:21.009 --> 00:38:22.886
Yeah. They hired me on the spot.

777
00:38:22.970 --> 00:38:26.306
I would've told you all sooner.
but I didn't wanna step on Tori's thing.

778
00:38:26.390 --> 00:38:28.684
and since it's no longer a thing. uh…

779
00:38:28.767 --> 00:38:29.768
Surprise. [chuckles]

780
00:38:29.852 --> 00:38:31.353
I thought we talked about this.

781
00:38:31.436 --> 00:38:33.313
- [quietly] We did and I told her--
- What is that now?

782
00:38:33.397 --> 00:38:34.898
- Nothing. It's…
- Nothing.

783
00:38:35.607 --> 00:38:38.151
He was worried it might be
too much for you. I disagreed.

784
00:38:38.902 --> 00:38:40.070
Ah.

785
00:38:40.153 --> 00:38:41.947
Hey. Andy. quick question.

786
00:38:42.030 --> 00:38:43.866
- What the fuck?
- Okay. You know what?

787
00:38:43.949 --> 00:38:45.534
Thanks for that. Thank you.

788
00:38:45.617 --> 00:38:47.661
All right.
so you're trying to control Ali too.

789
00:38:47.744 --> 00:38:50.789
Does anyone ever age out. or is it
just your plan to control us all forever?

790
00:38:51.373 --> 00:38:55.544
Tori. I just wanna say
this is the same age that Ali was

791
00:38:55.627 --> 00:38:58.130
when she started to rebel.
and look what happened to her.

792
00:38:58.213 --> 00:39:00.465
- Mom. Mom. Not…
- There it is.

793
00:39:00.549 --> 00:39:02.885
- Not a great time for this.
- Don't pay any attention to her.

794
00:39:02.968 --> 00:39:05.304
- We're very proud of you.
- I'm just trying to help.

795
00:39:05.387 --> 00:39:07.472
- Yeah. maybe try a little less. dear.
- [groans]

796
00:39:07.556 --> 00:39:11.101
You just can't handle the fact that
I'm not following the exact path you did.

797
00:39:11.768 --> 00:39:16.481
Sweetheart. college is where you go
to find your path.

798
00:39:17.149 --> 00:39:19.276
Right. okay. And how has
that worked out for you and Dad?

799
00:39:20.360 --> 00:39:22.946
What? Because we…
Because our marriage didn't work out?

800
00:39:23.030 --> 00:39:25.741
- Is that what this is about?
- No. your lives didn't work out.

801
00:39:26.575 --> 00:39:27.951
Okay. you lost your job.

802
00:39:28.035 --> 00:39:29.077
You both did.

803
00:39:29.870 --> 00:39:32.915
And now. you're starting over
and Mom thinks she's gonna write a book.

804
00:39:32.998 --> 00:39:35.167
Okay. Tori. cool it. all right?

805
00:39:35.250 --> 00:39:36.335
[sighs]

806
00:39:36.418 --> 00:39:39.922
Okay. So. what is your grand plan?

807
00:39:40.964 --> 00:39:41.965
I don't have a plan yet.

808
00:39:42.049 --> 00:39:44.593
You're not giving me any room
to breathe or figure it out.

809
00:39:46.011 --> 00:39:47.137
I need some air.

810
00:39:47.221 --> 00:39:49.097
- Baby. I--
- [Tori] Don't follow me.

811
00:39:51.433 --> 00:39:52.559
[sighs]

812
00:39:52.643 --> 00:39:54.645
[pensive music plays]

813
00:40:00.150 --> 00:40:01.151
Hey.

814
00:40:07.908 --> 00:40:09.159
She's doing this to punish us.

815
00:40:10.494 --> 00:40:11.662
It might not be about us.

816
00:40:11.745 --> 00:40:13.288
Of course it's about us.

817
00:40:14.039 --> 00:40:15.582
Look at the last year she's had.

818
00:40:15.666 --> 00:40:18.669
This is a classic trauma response
to the whole mess you got us into.

819
00:40:18.752 --> 00:40:20.003
[scoffs] Really?

820
00:40:24.967 --> 00:40:29.054
I'm sorry.
I'm just… just spinning out here.

821
00:40:31.765 --> 00:40:34.184
Maybe there is something to
what Tori is actually saying.

822
00:40:35.519 --> 00:40:38.689
- You're on her side?
- I'm not on anyone's side.

823
00:40:38.772 --> 00:40:41.775
I'm not taking sides.
I'm just saying. let's hear her out.

824
00:40:41.859 --> 00:40:44.236
This is not the time to
treat her like a rational actor.

825
00:40:44.319 --> 00:40:47.906
She's being reckless and rebellious
and she's gonna blow up her whole life.

826
00:40:48.407 --> 00:40:50.909
Maybe. And maybe we have to let her.

827
00:40:51.869 --> 00:40:52.870
Don't do that.

828
00:40:53.453 --> 00:40:54.955
This isn't Ali.

829
00:40:55.455 --> 00:40:59.293
You can't tell me not to parent
my own daughter. our daughter.

830
00:40:59.376 --> 00:41:00.627
[muffled music playing]

831
00:41:07.759 --> 00:41:09.678
You have the wrong driveway.

832
00:41:11.180 --> 00:41:12.181
They're here for me.

833
00:41:13.223 --> 00:41:15.309
- What do you mean?
- Just going to a concert with Delilah.

834
00:41:15.392 --> 00:41:18.520
Wha… [stammers] Excuse me. with who?

835
00:41:19.938 --> 00:41:20.939
Hey. hey.

836
00:41:21.481 --> 00:41:22.482
Oh.

837
00:41:22.566 --> 00:41:23.567
[chuckles]

838
00:41:24.568 --> 00:41:25.903
Hey. Delilah. say hi.

839
00:41:29.198 --> 00:41:31.491
Coop. Melanie. Great to see ya.

840
00:41:32.492 --> 00:41:35.954
I'll have him home by midnight. maybe.

841
00:41:39.791 --> 00:41:41.043
- Hey.
- Hey.

842
00:41:42.794 --> 00:41:46.798
Sorry about that and this
and everything to come.

843
00:41:46.882 --> 00:41:49.218
Trust me. it's way better than
what's going on in my house.

844
00:41:49.301 --> 00:41:51.386
Hey. Hunter! You ready to rock?

845
00:41:51.470 --> 00:41:53.847
Dad. please take it down several notches.

846
00:41:53.931 --> 00:41:55.474
What was that? Sorry. I can't hear you.

847
00:41:56.391 --> 00:41:57.601
You're like a mile away.

848
00:41:58.393 --> 00:42:00.187
[laughs] Maybe just call me.

849
00:42:01.813 --> 00:42:03.690
I don't trust that guy.

850
00:42:04.274 --> 00:42:05.484
Certainly is friendly.

851
00:42:07.236 --> 00:42:08.237
Where are you going?

852
00:42:09.530 --> 00:42:11.406
To find her and get to the bottom of this.

853
00:42:11.490 --> 00:42:12.866
Just give her some space. huh?

854
00:42:13.450 --> 00:42:14.993
[chuckles] I know you mean well.

855
00:42:15.077 --> 00:42:18.622
but getting parenting advice from you
is really hard right now.

856
00:42:19.456 --> 00:42:21.124
Yeah. and your way is working really well.

857
00:42:21.208 --> 00:42:23.961
If you wanna be helpful.
go in there and get rid of your family.

858
00:42:26.922 --> 00:42:28.507
I'm just… Not you. Ron.

859
00:42:29.091 --> 00:42:30.092
Course not.

860
00:42:30.968 --> 00:42:31.969
[exhales]

861
00:42:34.012 --> 00:42:35.472
Hey. Dad. [sighs]

862
00:42:35.556 --> 00:42:36.974
Sorry you had to witness that.

863
00:42:37.933 --> 00:42:38.934
That?

864
00:42:39.810 --> 00:42:41.061
That was nothing.

865
00:42:46.108 --> 00:42:47.568
It's hard when you reach the point where

866
00:42:47.651 --> 00:42:49.862
you can't protect your kids
the way you used to.

867
00:42:49.945 --> 00:42:52.906
Not from the world.
not from their own choices.

868
00:42:54.157 --> 00:42:57.160
I'm her father.
If I can't protect her. then who?

869
00:42:57.786 --> 00:43:00.414
Well. it's not that you can't.
It's that she won't let you.

870
00:43:00.497 --> 00:43:01.331
[sighs]

871
00:43:01.415 --> 00:43:04.585
Because you've raised a smart
and fiercely independent daughter.

872
00:43:04.668 --> 00:43:08.297
Which doesn't mean she is not gonna
screw up. She will. a lot.

873
00:43:09.339 --> 00:43:12.342
And that's when being a father
becomes really tricky.

874
00:43:12.426 --> 00:43:14.887
because it's no longer about
telling her what to do.

875
00:43:14.970 --> 00:43:15.971
[sighs]

876
00:43:16.054 --> 00:43:21.560
It's about finding a way to let go
while still keeping everyone close.

877
00:43:22.186 --> 00:43:24.688
She's making choices that
are gonna wreck her life.

878
00:43:24.771 --> 00:43:29.693
That's the hardest part
because your job is no longer to stop her.

879
00:43:29.776 --> 00:43:32.613
Your job is to stay on the sidelines.

880
00:43:33.322 --> 00:43:34.990
Just make sure she knows
you're there for her

881
00:43:35.073 --> 00:43:36.783
when she realizes she needs you.

882
00:43:39.328 --> 00:43:40.329
[exhales]

883
00:43:45.000 --> 00:43:46.251
Well. I'm glad you're here.

884
00:43:46.877 --> 00:43:48.879
- Thanks.
- [grunts]

885
00:43:50.339 --> 00:43:52.424
- You coming? [sighs]
- Give me five more minutes.

886
00:43:52.508 --> 00:43:53.884
I could use a break from your mother.

887
00:43:53.967 --> 00:43:55.552
Jesus. Take ten.

888
00:43:55.636 --> 00:43:56.845
[chuckles. sniffles]

889
00:43:57.804 --> 00:43:59.223
[Coop sighs]

890
00:44:21.119 --> 00:44:22.120
[squelching]

891
00:44:23.830 --> 00:44:26.041
[gasps. screams]

892
00:44:30.712 --> 00:44:34.550
Fuck you! [panting]

893
00:44:36.635 --> 00:44:37.636
Not you.

894
00:44:44.810 --> 00:44:47.813
[Coop] I was dealing with an aching back
and a familial clusterfuck.

895
00:44:47.896 --> 00:44:49.773
So. I wasn't really in the mood to work.

896
00:44:50.524 --> 00:44:53.819
but this job didn't come with sick days
or paid family leave.

897
00:44:54.611 --> 00:44:55.612
And the fact was.

898
00:44:55.696 --> 00:44:57.990
I knew Ashe and his daughter
were out for the night

899
00:44:58.073 --> 00:44:59.157
and that he hadn't staffed up yet.

900
00:44:59.241 --> 00:45:00.993
So. there was a window we couldn't ignore.

901
00:45:06.290 --> 00:45:08.542
I also knew his house had a lot of doors.

902
00:45:08.625 --> 00:45:10.752
and he didn't seem like
the kind of guy who would do a circuit

903
00:45:10.836 --> 00:45:12.504
to make sure they were all locked.

904
00:45:16.967 --> 00:45:17.968
[clicks]

905
00:45:18.969 --> 00:45:20.220
Okay. I got a door.

906
00:45:22.222 --> 00:45:25.475
You're absolutely positive
there's no security system installed yet?

907
00:45:25.559 --> 00:45:28.604
He is taking bids from Héctor's company
and two others next week.

908
00:45:28.687 --> 00:45:29.980
[Coop] Staff?

909
00:45:30.063 --> 00:45:32.149
I already told you
he hired Hennah's cousin.

910
00:45:32.232 --> 00:45:33.859
and she starts tomorrow.

911
00:45:38.155 --> 00:45:39.239
You're being quiet.

912
00:45:39.865 --> 00:45:40.949
It's been a long night.

913
00:45:41.491 --> 00:45:43.952
- You wanna talk about it?
- Not particularly.

914
00:45:44.036 --> 00:45:45.871
Good. Let's talk about Barney then.

915
00:45:47.289 --> 00:45:48.415
What about him?

916
00:45:48.498 --> 00:45:53.086
I just… I don't understand why
you wanna bring more people into this.

917
00:45:53.170 --> 00:45:54.213
[Coop] Because he's right.

918
00:45:54.296 --> 00:45:56.465
If we keep working at this clip.

919
00:45:56.548 --> 00:45:58.884
we're gonna need to find some way

920
00:45:58.967 --> 00:46:00.719
to make all this money
we're earning look legit.

921
00:46:00.802 --> 00:46:05.140
Otherwise. we're gonna be sitting
on piles of cash that we can't use.

922
00:46:05.724 --> 00:46:08.185
Well. where I live. cash is still king.

923
00:46:08.268 --> 00:46:09.645
We might not need Barney yet.

924
00:46:09.728 --> 00:46:11.813
but there's only so much money
you can stuff under a mattress.

925
00:46:11.897 --> 00:46:14.483
[chuckles] I don't know. Coop.

926
00:46:14.566 --> 00:46:17.152
It sounds to me like
you're still trying to have it both ways.

927
00:46:17.694 --> 00:46:19.196
What is that supposed to mean?

928
00:46:19.988 --> 00:46:22.241
You're a thief and you want a 401(k).

929
00:46:22.908 --> 00:46:26.078
I think you need to decide who you are
and be that person.

930
00:46:26.703 --> 00:46:28.372
I contain multitudes.

931
00:46:28.956 --> 00:46:30.374
Multitudes of bullshit.

932
00:46:30.874 --> 00:46:32.835
All right. Elena. look.

933
00:46:32.918 --> 00:46:36.213
Barney is consulting for us like Héctor.
And you're my only partner.

934
00:46:40.092 --> 00:46:41.093
Fine.

935
00:46:42.386 --> 00:46:44.638
Maybe it is time that I got
the white guy treatment.

936
00:46:44.721 --> 00:46:45.848
like you and Barney.

937
00:46:46.431 --> 00:46:48.016
Okay. You know. Barney is not white.

938
00:46:48.642 --> 00:46:50.018
Mmm. Does he know that?

939
00:46:59.695 --> 00:47:02.030
[Coop] Edith Wharton's The House of Mirth.

940
00:47:02.114 --> 00:47:04.616
Signed. first edition. first printing.
American issue

941
00:47:04.700 --> 00:47:06.869
with frontispiece
and seven illustrated plates.

942
00:47:06.952 --> 00:47:11.540
Pristine condition. with an estimated
value of up to $115.000 at auction.

943
00:47:11.623 --> 00:47:15.043
And it's not even her masterpiece.
that would be The Age of Innocence.

944
00:47:15.127 --> 00:47:18.589
That one that made her the first woman
to win a Pulitzer Prize for fiction.

945
00:47:18.672 --> 00:47:21.842
Well. she technically only won
after the jury's original selection.

946
00:47:21.925 --> 00:47:24.553
Sinclair Lewis's Main Street.
was disqualified.

947
00:47:25.262 --> 00:47:27.347
Not that it mattered
to collectors like Ashe.

948
00:47:27.431 --> 00:47:29.933
Who had almost certainly
never even cracked the spine.

949
00:47:30.017 --> 00:47:33.645
These books were purchased by the yard.
probably by a book stylist.

950
00:47:33.729 --> 00:47:36.732
Just another way to dress his walls
with appreciating assets.

951
00:47:37.608 --> 00:47:40.277
- [Elena] Coop.
- Yeah. Yeah. I got it.

952
00:47:41.653 --> 00:47:42.738
I'm coming out.

953
00:47:45.157 --> 00:47:46.742
All right.
You're showing some healthy gains.

954
00:47:46.825 --> 00:47:48.327
but you need to diversify
a little bit more.

955
00:47:48.410 --> 00:47:50.329
And for God's sake.
stop investing in T-bills.

956
00:47:50.412 --> 00:47:52.039
You're just leaving money on the table.

957
00:47:52.122 --> 00:47:54.124
- You get that SEP IRA set up yet?
- [door slams]

958
00:47:56.043 --> 00:47:57.169
Talk to her.

959
00:47:57.794 --> 00:47:59.004
You need the shelter.

960
00:48:02.466 --> 00:48:03.467
[door buzzes]

961
00:48:12.184 --> 00:48:14.520
Quit rabble-rousing. Coop.

962
00:48:15.354 --> 00:48:17.397
What do you have for me today?

963
00:48:19.525 --> 00:48:20.359
Hmm.

964
00:48:21.443 --> 00:48:22.528
Edith Wharton.

965
00:48:28.408 --> 00:48:29.618
First edition.

966
00:48:31.578 --> 00:48:33.080
Excellent condition.

967
00:48:35.249 --> 00:48:36.750
Well. I can move this.

968
00:48:38.293 --> 00:48:40.712
I always preferred Jane Austen myself.

969
00:48:41.588 --> 00:48:43.340
[inhales sharply]
I would not have called that.

970
00:48:44.049 --> 00:48:45.551
We were all young once.

971
00:48:46.343 --> 00:48:47.344
What about you?

972
00:48:48.303 --> 00:48:49.513
I'm more of a movie guy.

973
00:48:49.596 --> 00:48:52.307
Ugh. that's what's wrong
with your generation.

974
00:48:52.891 --> 00:48:55.602
No appreciation for the finer arts.

975
00:48:56.311 --> 00:48:58.897
Speaking of. did you find a buyer
for the Bacon yet?

976
00:48:59.439 --> 00:49:01.275
Still too hot. [chuckles]

977
00:49:02.025 --> 00:49:07.865
The owner has done everything
short of alerting Interpol

978
00:49:07.948 --> 00:49:09.199
that it was stolen.

979
00:49:10.576 --> 00:49:12.661
You're gonna have to sit on it
for a while.

980
00:49:13.245 --> 00:49:14.872
Maybe even another year.

981
00:49:15.914 --> 00:49:17.207
What if I don't have another year?

982
00:49:17.291 --> 00:49:19.793
- [phone ringing]
- Then you'll probably end up in prison.

983
00:49:21.461 --> 00:49:22.462
[exhales deeply]

984
00:49:24.464 --> 00:49:26.091
Hey. Barney.
I'm right in the middle of something.

985
00:49:26.175 --> 00:49:27.593
Can I call you back in like ten?

986
00:49:27.676 --> 00:49:29.303
[Barney]
Okay. but actually call me back for once.

987
00:49:29.386 --> 00:49:31.889
I may have found a solution
to our little logistics problem.

988
00:49:36.560 --> 00:49:37.686
Sorry about that. [sighs]

989
00:49:37.769 --> 00:49:39.479
Always be closing. right?

990
00:49:39.563 --> 00:49:41.899
[chuckles] Mamet. Nice.

991
00:49:43.984 --> 00:49:47.654
Thank you for this.
I have to get back to work.

992
00:49:50.240 --> 00:49:51.533
[stammers] Sidney.

993
00:49:51.617 --> 00:49:52.701
Later. Frank.

994
00:50:05.631 --> 00:50:08.050
[J.J.] Harvey. I often wish I were deaf
and wore a hearing aid.

995
00:50:08.133 --> 00:50:09.468
With a simple flick of a switch.

996
00:50:09.551 --> 00:50:12.262
I could shut out
the greedy murmur of little men.

997
00:50:12.346 --> 00:50:14.056
[Sidney]
J.J.. I need your ear for two minutes.

998
00:50:14.139 --> 00:50:15.140
- [J.J.] Mac!
- [Mac] Yes?

999
00:50:15.224 --> 00:50:16.433
[J.J.] I don't want this man at my table…

1000
00:50:16.517 --> 00:50:17.851
[Sidney]
I've got a message from your sister.

1001
00:50:18.435 --> 00:50:20.687
- [humming]
- [whirring]

1002
00:50:23.732 --> 00:50:24.733
Hey. Coop.

1003
00:50:26.527 --> 00:50:27.778
Ashe. what are you doing here?

1004
00:50:29.321 --> 00:50:31.240
Hey. did Hunter have a good time
at the show?

1005
00:50:31.865 --> 00:50:33.825
He's a really. really nice kid.

1006
00:50:33.909 --> 00:50:36.328
Little quiet. but polite.

1007
00:50:37.329 --> 00:50:39.915
And I think my daughter may have
a little crush on him. [chuckles]

1008
00:50:39.998 --> 00:50:40.999
[chuckles]

1009
00:50:41.583 --> 00:50:42.876
Is there something I can help you with?

1010
00:50:42.960 --> 00:50:45.045
I don't mean to be rude.
but I got a bunch of calls and…

1011
00:50:45.921 --> 00:50:46.922
Yeah.

1012
00:50:48.257 --> 00:50:50.551
Remember when I told you
you're a complicated guy?

1013
00:50:51.760 --> 00:50:52.761
Yeah.

1014
00:50:53.554 --> 00:50:58.308
Well. it turns out.
I had no idea how complicated.

1015
00:51:05.858 --> 00:51:07.734
[exhales deeply]

1015
00:51:08.305 --> 00:52:08.468
